! WYCKOFF_INFORMATION_END
!=====================================================================================!
END

[EDITOR] Yoshihisa Ishikawa (IMSS, KEK)

@attention : Some keys have already been reserved .
[DELIMITER] ";", because the "," has been used by the notation of atomic coordinates in component.
[RESERVED WORDS]
"#"   : Using for Serial ID
"!"   : Comment out (In particular, used by first word in sentence)
"END" : Break Point of this database. 

@param : This database has been describes by two blocks for each space groups, thus Header and Wyckoff component, respectively.
[Header Part : 12 elements]
#ID       :  Serial ID 
ZR_ID     :  Space group ID using Z-Rietveld
enum_SPG  :  enum ID using Z-Rietveld  (since ver 0.2.0)
ZMEM_NUM  :  Space group ID for Z-MEM [@attention Not yet defined strictly]
HM_NORMAL :  Hermann–Mauguin Symbol 
HM_FULL   :  Full notation of Hermann–Mauguin symbol
SPG_NO    :  Space group Number (1 - 230)
ORIGIN    :  Origin Choice (0/1)
AXIS      :  Unique axis or Permutation (Orthorhombic), "-" means NULL
INV       :  haveInversion_Symmetry
LATT      :  Lattice Type P/A/B/C/I/F/H/R
ELEMENT_NUM means the component counts of Site Symmetry block

[Component Part]
  MULTIPLICITY;  Multiplicity of site symmetry (with Taranslation of Sublattice) 
WYCKOFF_LETTER;  Wyckoff letter
 SITE_SYMMETRY;  Site symmetry notation
COORDINATES[] ;  Array. coordinates in each site symmetry.

@brief
1. First 534 space groups are listed by the unique symmetry operation, which is considered the unique axis and permutation (orthorhombic group). 
   Second set means the equivalent symmetry operation for first set. 
   Third one would be described as the "alias", which is mainly used by another notation of "n / e" glide operation (In future version).
2. Space group ordering in data list is based on the definition of Z-Rietveld.
3.  Z-MEM_ID has been put as the temporary notation in order to distinguish overlapped notation in Z-R_ID, 
    so that it will change in future version. I reccomend not to use this term.
4. In trigonal/Hexagonal froups, the notation of lattice type "H" means as the hexagonal setting with attached three translation vectors, 
   "R" is rhombohedral settings without translation vector.
5. If you find mistake in this table, please tell us.

